/* --- The failure paths, 12 Sep 2026 --------------------------------------
   Every one of these was Finnish on an English phone, and the check could not
   see one of them: each sat in a ternary, an assignment or a returned String
   rather than as the argument of a Text. They are almost all errors, alerts
   and empty states — which is why the demo video surfaced only four of this
   kind. The happy path is the one that gets demonstrated, and nobody
   demonstrates a failure.

   Found with a scan over every Finnish literal in the Swift source minus the
   two tables, not by opening screens: 338 literals, 254 already held, 84 in
   neither. Of the 84 the ones that stay Finnish are data rather than
   interface — QuestionLadder's matching patterns, the seed fixture's told
   content, and the author names and extracted questions that are WRITTEN INTO
   THE ARCHIVE, where an English word would be somebody's record of their own
   family. */
